{
  "_comment": "REVIEWED. Utah committee-minutes printed names → PolitiDex politician ids, for the 2025 General Session. This file exists because committee minutes print a member a third way. The roster prints a full name, the floor vote pages print \"Surname, Initials\", and a committee vote line prints \"Rep. T. Auxier\" — prefix, initials, surname. Every entry below was accepted by hand; the tool proposes and never writes here. See db/vr-ingest-runbook.md § Utah.",
  "_howReviewed": "Two ways in, and nothing else was accepted. (1) exact_floor_key: the transposed printed form lands exactly on a key in db/vr-utah-member-map.json, which is itself a hand-reviewed file confirmed against the legislature`s roster for 2025 (roster.asp?year=2025). 87 of the 96 forms resolved this way and inherit that review. (2) unique_surname_confirmed_by_attendance: the printed initials are shorter than the floor key`s, so the two do not meet. Those 9 were resolved only where the surname is unique in that chamber`s floor map AND the SAME meeting`s own attendance list names exactly one member with that surname AND that attendance line`s full name agrees with both the vote line`s initials and the floor key`s. `confirmedBy` records the attendance line that did it. Representative Walter is the case that made this necessary: the committee prints \"Rep. R. Walter\", the floor page prints \"Walter, N.\", and only the attendance line \"Rep. R. Neil Walter\" shows that those are one person. Neither initial could have been derived from the other.",
  "_unmappedIsCoverage": "`unmapped` is empty for this session, and that is a fact about 2025, not a rule: every printed name on an admitted 2025 committee vote resolved. If a later session leaves names here they are a COVERAGE GAP — votes not written — and they are never folded in with the refusals below.",
  "_refusalNotes": "`_refusedNames` is empty for this session because no 2025 committee vote line was ambiguous. It is not empty in principle. db/vr-utah-member-map-2024GS.json and -2023GS.json each refuse \"Judkins, M.\" and \"Lyman, P.\": resolving those would rest on a guess about which human the printed name is. A name of that class stays REFUSED here too — a committee minute is not a second chance to attribute it.",
  "session": "2025GS",
